node_modules/
package-lock.json
pnpm-lock.yaml
*.tgz
*.log
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Build output, with one deliberate exception: the offline page is the product's
# promise ("download it, double-click it, no Node needed"), so that ONE file is
# committed. `dist/*` instead of `dist/` because git cannot re-include a file inside
# an excluded directory. web-selftest.mjs rebuilds and byte-compares it, so a stale
# committed copy fails the test instead of shipping.
dist/*
!dist/tradzh.html

# Machine-private deny-list for scripts/api-selftest.mjs's shipped-file scan. It must stay
# untracked: the file exists precisely to keep those names out of anything that ships.
.ship-deny.txt

# The board plugin's per-workspace output. It holds ABSOLUTE PATHS by design (the board has to
# say which directory it read), and the leak scan deliberately skips it for that reason - so
# ignoring it here is what keeps that skip honest. Found 2026-09-22: it was untracked but NOT
# ignored, i.e. one `git add -A` away from publishing `C:\Users\...` into a public repo, and the
# scan could not have warned (it skips the directory). scripts/api-selftest.mjs now FAILS if a
# skipped directory is not listed here.
.board/
